       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. You've confirmed it, but 2000 mg of sertraline daily is 10 times the maximum dose of 200 mg/day. I can't think of a clinical reason for it, and it would put the patient at serious risk of toxicity. Pharmacy and the order-entry system would normally flag it as well.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Tell me the dose, for example 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Add a note to the order.** If there is an unusual rationale, such as a dose that was already worked out with psychiatry or toxicology, give me the details. I can include them in a note, but I'd still want pharmacy to verify the dose before it's entered.\n- **Call pharmacy or the clinical pharmacist.** They can review the dose with you.\n\nIf you think this patient was already exposed to a very large amount of sertraline, such as an ingestion or overdose, that needs a toxicology or poison control consult (1-800-222-1222 in the US). It isn't a standing order."
      }
     ],
